wayland/screencopy: read the output transform without a QtWayland wl_output

OutputTransformQuery bound the output as a QtWayland::wl_output. Qt's
QWaylandScreen::fromWlOutput accepts any of those, so wl_surface.enter for
that binding put a fake QWaylandScreen in the surface's screen list, and
QWaylandSurface::oldestEnteredScreen crashed reading it once the real
screen left. Bind a plain wl_output with a listener of its own instead.
Applied by packaging/nix/nova-ui.nix (IMP-262).

